\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The pipeline. Only the two shaded boxes run a neural network, and both are used frozen: no training and no fine-tuning. Offline, each clip is decoded at 1\,fps and every sampled frame becomes a 512-dimensional unit vector, so the index is a single $N\times 512$ matrix. Online, a query costs one text embedding, one matrix--vector product and a max over the frames of each clip. Labels give measured per-unit costs (Section~IV).}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{2}{The pipeline. Only the two shaded boxes run a neural network, and both are used frozen: no training and no fine-tuning. Offline, each clip is decoded at 1\,fps and every sampled frame becomes a 512-dimensional unit vector, so the index is a single $N\times 512$ matrix. Online, a query costs one text embedding, one matrix--vector product and a max over the frames of each clip. Labels give measured per-unit costs (Section~IV)}{figure.1}{}}
