\newlabel{tab:fps}{{IV}{4}{Sampling-rate ablation on MSR-VTT ($n=1{,}000$ queries). The standard error of Recall@1 is $\approx $1.5\,pp, so adjacent rows are not distinguishable}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Accuracy versus indexing cost on MSR-VTT test 1k (zero-shot CLIP ViT-B/32, exhaustive search). Each point is a different frame-sampling rate; the horizontal axis is the measured indexing time for the same 1{,}000 clips (log scale). Varying the sampling rate over an 8$\times $ range changes indexing cost by 6.3$\times $ but Recall@1 by only 1.5\,pp, which is within one standard error (shaded band). Higher sampling rates therefore buy no measurable accuracy, placing the knee of the curve at 1\,fps.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cost}{{2}{4}{Accuracy versus indexing cost on MSR-VTT test 1k (zero-shot CLIP ViT-B/32, exhaustive search). Each point is a different frame-sampling rate; the horizontal axis is the measured indexing time for the same 1{,}000 clips (log scale). Varying the sampling rate over an 8$\times $ range changes indexing cost by 6.3$\times $ but Recall@1 by only 1.5\,pp, which is within one standard error (shaded band). Higher sampling rates therefore buy no measurable accuracy, placing the knee of the curve at 1\,fps}{figure.2}{}}
